.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WPA_PASSPHRASE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wpa_passphrase
.Nd make a network block with a WPA pre-shared key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar ssid
.Op Ar passphrase
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
computes the 256-bit pre-shared key of a WPA or WPA2 network from its name
.Ar ssid
and its
.Ar passphrase ,
of 8 to 63 printable ASCII characters, by PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA1 and 4096
iterations, and prints a
.Cm network
block for
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5
that holds the key, with the passphrase in a comment.
Without
.Ar passphrase ,
it reads one line from the standard input.
.Pp
A WPA3 network with SAE needs the passphrase itself, given as
.Cm sae_password
or
.Cm psk
in quotes; the key this computes serves only WPA and WPA2.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
The test vector of IEEE 802.11:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wpa_passphrase IEEE password
network={
	ssid="IEEE"
	#psk="password"
	psk=f42c6fc52df0ebef9ebb4b90b38a5f902e83fe1b135a70e23aed762e9710a12e
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
.Sh STANDARDS
IEEE 802.11-2020, annex J.4, and RFC 8018.
